{"source": "/home/ubuntu/shiva-study-set/Shiva Sutras 3.33.mp3", "engine": "faster-whisper-base", "segments": [{"t": 0.0, "end": 6.38, "text": "I see yogina for sathayogi sukdukhwar bairmananam."}, {"t": 6.38, "end": 12.02, "text": "The state of pleasure and dukhwurd in the state of pain."}, {"t": 12.02, "end": 16.52, "text": "In the state of pleasure and in the state of pain,"}, {"t": 16.52, "end": 19.78, "text": "for sathayogi bairmananam."}, {"t": 19.78, "end": 23.06, "text": "Bairmananam is there."}, {"t": 23.06, "end": 33.18, "text": "Bairmananam means he experiences the state of joy"}, {"t": 33.18, "end": 38.9, "text": "or the state of sadness, not with eye consciousness,"}, {"t": 38.9, "end": 42.7, "text": "but by this consciousness."}, {"t": 42.7, "end": 45.34, "text": "This is joy."}, {"t": 45.34, "end": 46.3, "text": "I am joyous."}, {"t": 46.3, "end": 49.22, "text": "He does not experience this way, that I am joyous."}, {"t": 49.22, "end": 51.82, "text": "He does not experience I am sad."}, {"t": 51.82, "end": 53.74, "text": "He experiences this sadness."}, {"t": 53.74, "end": 56.22, "text": "This is joy."}, {"t": 56.22, "end": 62.26, "text": "Just as you experience in ordinary daily routine of life,"}, {"t": 62.34, "end": 65.66, "text": "this is a part, this is a bottle, this is..."}, {"t": 65.66, "end": 69.26, "text": "You do not experience it with eye consciousness."}, {"t": 69.26, "end": 81.18, "text": "For sathayogi, he does not experience his joy and sadness with eye consciousness."}, {"t": 81.18, "end": 89.62, "text": "But on the contrary, by this consciousness, he experiences his joy and his sadness,"}, {"t": 89.66, "end": 94.5, "text": "just like an object, separate from his being."}, {"t": 94.5, "end": 99.5, "text": "In the state of pleasure and dukhwurd,"}, {"t": 99.5, "end": 103.02, "text": "these states, these two states of yogi,"}, {"t": 103.02, "end": 107.55, "text": "sook and dukh, pleasure and pain,"}, {"t": 107.55, "end": 110.15, "text": "or with the state of pleasure and dukhwurd,"}, {"t": 110.15, "end": 112.19, "text": "or just like with the state of pleasure,"}, {"t": 112.19, "end": 119.99, "text": "not with the state of pleasure, it has no type of nowhere."}, {"t": 119.99, "end": 122.91, "text": "It has... it... it... it... the..."}, {"t": 122.91, "end": 128.46, "text": "no one has touched it, not no worship."}, {"t": 128.46, "end": 133.7, "text": "So his sook and his dukh is just like another object,"}, {"t": 133.7, "end": 136.46, "text": "just like a stove."}, {"t": 136.46, "end": 137.18, "text": "What to mean?"}, {"t": 137.18, "end": 140.46, "text": "This is stove outside, outside me."}, {"t": 140.46, "end": 141.62, "text": "What have to do with this?"}, {"t": 141.62, "end": 143.3, "text": "Or this is pleasure?"}, {"t": 143.3, "end": 143.98, "text": "What to mean?"}, {"t": 143.98, "end": 147.36, "text": "This is pain, what to mean?"}, {"t": 147.36, "end": 151.28, "text": "Just like nila deva, just like other objects."}, {"t": 151.32, "end": 154.56, "text": "Yadantavas, they are by thisness, by this consciousness."}, {"t": 154.56, "end": 158.96, "text": "He experiences that sook and dukh, pleasure and pain."}, {"t": 158.96, "end": 163.2, "text": "Maninam means some way that I'm... he... to experience it."}, {"t": 163.2, "end": 167.36, "text": "Nathu, Lahu Kikavath, Ahantas, Persianian."}, {"t": 167.36, "end": 170.68, "text": "He does not experience sook and dukh, pleasure and pain,"}, {"t": 170.68, "end": 173.72, "text": "just like other ignorant people,"}, {"t": 173.72, "end": 177.52, "text": "putting one's eye consciousness in that."}, {"t": 177.52, "end": 182.76, "text": "That, I am happy, I am sad."}, {"t": 182.76, "end": 185.56, "text": "I am never happy, I am never sad."}, {"t": 185.56, "end": 189.84, "text": "I am always in myself, same."}, {"t": 189.84, "end": 192.72, "text": "In happiness and his sadness."}, {"t": 192.72, "end": 196.68, "text": "Asi, he sushaktipratiyosivisham yatu ktu sutra arthnidya"}, {"t": 196.68, "end": 199.64, "text": "sarvam-antas-chhajita-dhe naosurati."}, {"t": 199.64, "end": 202.84, "text": "Because for such a yogi,"}, {"t": 202.84, "end": 206.44, "text": "as it is explained in this sushaktipratiyosivisham,"}, {"t": 206.48, "end": 212.44, "text": "this whole universe is the expansion of his own energies."}, {"t": 212.44, "end": 216.32, "text": "Yatu ktu sutra arthnidya, by this explanation,"}, {"t": 216.32, "end": 219.36, "text": "sarvam-antas-chhajita-dhe naosurati."}, {"t": 219.36, "end": 226.32, "text": "He experiences this whole universe with eye consciousness,"}, {"t": 226.32, "end": 230.97, "text": "individuality with this consciousness."}, {"t": 230.97, "end": 235.09, "text": "Because he is never individual being, he is always universal being."}, {"t": 235.09, "end": 240.01, "text": "He experiences his nature as universal being."}, {"t": 240.09, "end": 246.25, "text": "He does not experience his nature as individual being."}, {"t": 246.25, "end": 249.65, "text": "If he would experience his nature as individual being,"}, {"t": 249.65, "end": 253.89, "text": "then he would get sad and happy."}, {"t": 253.89, "end": 256.77, "text": "Happiness and sadness would shine there then."}, {"t": 256.77, "end": 259.49, "text": "If there was individuality,"}, {"t": 259.49, "end": 264.49, "text": "as long as it is proved that his being is universal."}, {"t": 266.93, "end": 270.97, "text": "If sadness is here, happiness is there."}, {"t": 271.97, "end": 275.97, "text": "If mere kaisam is sad,"}, {"t": 275.97, "end": 279.37, "text": "bhakshigulam mamat or sheikhs are happy."}, {"t": 279.37, "end": 281.57, "text": "So, I am happy. I am sad."}, {"t": 281.57, "end": 284.17, "text": "I am everything. I am universal."}, {"t": 284.17, "end": 285.97, "text": "What of that?"}, {"t": 285.97, "end": 288.97, "text": "Sadness is here and"}, {"t": 288.97, "end": 292.97, "text": "because this is the real fullness of being."}, {"t": 292.97, "end": 294.97, "text": "If you take experience."}, {"t": 294.97, "end": 297.97, "text": "You will never get sad or you will never get happy."}, {"t": 297.97, "end": 302.97, "text": "If you experience this state in a universal way."}, {"t": 302.97, "end": 311.17, "text": "In an individual way, everything is shank."}, {"t": 311.17, "end": 315.17, "text": "Natu natham sukudukhyadeva, itevan param etat."}, {"t": 315.17, "end": 320.17, "text": "It is not, this sutra is not meant for Sukhandukh only."}, {"t": 320.17, "end": 324.17, "text": "For everything, whatever exists in this world,"}, {"t": 324.17, "end": 333.63, "text": "he experiences it either with this consciousness."}, {"t": 333.63, "end": 336.63, "text": "In individual state of way."}, {"t": 336.63, "end": 341.63, "text": "If he remains in universal state of way,"}, {"t": 341.63, "end": 345.63, "text": "then he experiences everything with eye consciousness."}, {"t": 345.63, "end": 349.87, "text": "I will be thinking."}, {"t": 349.87, "end": 352.87, "text": "Yogi, he preshant parishtakapramatri bhava."}, {"t": 352.87, "end": 356.87, "text": "Because yogi has destroyed the state of"}, {"t": 356.87, "end": 358.87, "text": "ainess on purishtaka."}, {"t": 358.87, "end": 361.87, "text": "Purishtaka does not mean only purishtaka."}, {"t": 361.87, "end": 364.87, "text": "Body, purishtaka and shunya."}, {"t": 364.87, "end": 365.87, "text": "Sushvati."}, {"t": 365.87, "end": 369.87, "text": "The state of the yapılness,"}, {"t": 369.87, "end": 371.87, "text": "the state of dreaming state,"}, {"t": 371.87, "end": 374.87, "text": "and the state of dreamless state."}, {"t": 374.87, "end": 378.87, "text": "But these three states are destroyed there,"}, {"t": 378.87, "end": 380.87, "text": "sub-sari."}, {"t": 380.87, "end": 386.87, "text": "Katham sukudukhyadeva, how can he be touched?"}, {"t": 386.87, "end": 390.87, "text": "How can these two states,"}, {"t": 390.87, "end": 393.87, "text": "pleasure and pain touch him?"}, {"t": 393.87, "end": 395.87, "text": "Make him worried."}, {"t": 395.87, "end": 399.87, "text": "Tathacharya Shri Prithvigya, Sutra Vyamarshanyam,"}, {"t": 399.87, "end": 403.87, "text": "Intika Shri Prithvigya, it is also said."}, {"t": 403.87, "end": 406.87, "text": "Grahagbhumika Uttirnana,"}, {"t": 406.87, "end": 410.87, "text": "those yogis who have crossed the state"}, {"t": 410.87, "end": 414.87, "text": "crossed the boundary of indiguality."}, {"t": 414.87, "end": 418.87, "text": "Grahagbhumika means the state of indiguality."}, {"t": 418.87, "end": 421.87, "text": "Those who have crossed the state of indiguality."}, {"t": 421.87, "end": 424.87, "text": "Vastav Pramatr Dasha Prabhannana,"}, {"t": 424.87, "end": 426.87, "text": "and who have achieved,"}, {"t": 426.87, "end": 428.87, "text": "the real,"}, {"t": 428.87, "end": 430.87, "text": "Vastav means the real Pramatr Dasha,"}, {"t": 430.87, "end": 432.87, "text": "the state of universal being,"}, {"t": 432.87, "end": 434.87, "text": "the state of universal being,"}, {"t": 434.87, "end": 438.87, "text": "who are established in the state of universality."}, {"t": 438.87, "end": 441.87, "text": "Tathacharya Uttasthapit,"}, {"t": 441.87, "end": 443.87, "text": "Sukudukhyasacharya Karebi,"}, {"t": 443.87, "end": 447.87, "text": "although they experience in their daily routine of life,"}, {"t": 447.87, "end": 449.87, "text": "pleasure and pain,"}, {"t": 449.87, "end": 452.87, "text": "do not affect them at all."}, {"t": 452.87, "end": 457.53, "text": "No Padde De Ewa Sukhadi,"}, {"t": 457.53, "end": 463.32, "text": "there is not no question of pain and pleasure"}, {"t": 463.32, "end": 466.32, "text": "to rise in them,"}, {"t": 466.32, "end": 469.32, "text": "because heathu-vaykalyaat,"}, {"t": 469.32, "end": 475.69, "text": "the rise, the cause of the rise of pain and pleasure"}, {"t": 475.69, "end": 478.69, "text": "is individual indiguality,"}, {"t": 478.69, "end": 481.69, "text": "and that indigatory they have destroyed."}, {"t": 481.69, "end": 484.69, "text": "Heathu-vaykalyaat,"}, {"t": 484.69, "end": 486.69, "text": "heathu is indiguality,"}, {"t": 486.69, "end": 491.22, "text": "experiment of indiguality,"}, {"t": 491.22, "end": 492.22, "text": "it is destroyed,"}, {"t": 492.22, "end": 493.22, "text": "vaykalyaat,"}, {"t": 493.22, "end": 494.22, "text": "it is destroyed,"}, {"t": 494.22, "end": 495.22, "text": "they are away from that,"}, {"t": 495.22, "end": 496.22, "text": "Sahaja Ananda,"}, {"t": 496.22, "end": 497.22, "text": "Ayurabhavastu,"}, {"t": 497.22, "end": 498.22, "text": "Tathacharya."}, {"t": 498.22, "end": 502.22, "text": "So, in pleasure and pain,"}, {"t": 502.22, "end": 508.22, "text": "they experience the real state of supreme,"}, {"t": 508.22, "end": 509.22, "text": "literature,"}, {"t": 509.22, "end": 512.22, "text": "supreme bliss,"}, {"t": 512.22, "end": 513.22, "text": "Ananda."}, {"t": 513.22, "end": 515.22, "text": "It is more than bliss."}, {"t": 515.22, "end": 518.66, "text": "At the other,"}, {"t": 518.66, "end": 520.66, "text": "it is why it is,"}, {"t": 520.66, "end": 522.66, "text": "in this connection,"}, {"t": 522.66, "end": 524.66, "text": "explain in Spanda,"}, {"t": 524.66, "end": 525.66, "text": "in this yoga,"}, {"t": 525.66, "end": 527.66, "text": "no adukam na sukhamyaatra,"}, {"t": 527.66, "end": 528.66, "text": "no graham,"}, {"t": 528.66, "end": 529.66, "text": "grah ko nature,"}, {"t": 529.66, "end": 530.66, "text": "na chasti,"}, {"t": 530.66, "end": 532.66, "text": "murubhavo, peetadasti,"}, {"t": 532.66, "end": 533.66, "text": "parmaatata."}, {"t": 533.66, "end": 536.66, "text": "That in reality exists"}, {"t": 536.66, "end": 539.66, "text": "in the universal state of,"}, {"t": 539.66, "end": 542.66, "text": "in that universal state,"}, {"t": 542.66, "end": 544.66, "text": "where there is no pain,"}, {"t": 544.66, "end": 545.66, "text": "no pleasure,"}, {"t": 545.66, "end": 546.66, "text": "no object,"}, {"t": 546.66, "end": 547.66, "text": "no subject,"}, {"t": 547.66, "end": 550.66, "text": "and not you,"}, {"t": 550.66, "end": 552.66, "text": "negation of the,"}, {"t": 552.66, "end": 554.66, "text": "na chasti, murubhavo, peetadasti,"}, {"t": 554.66, "end": 555.66, "text": "negation of the,"}, {"t": 555.66, "end": 556.66, "text": "negation of sukh,"}, {"t": 556.66, "end": 557.66, "text": "duq, pleasure and pain,"}, {"t": 557.66, "end": 559.66, "text": "and objectivity,"}, {"t": 559.66, "end": 560.66, "text": "and subjectivity."}]}